OL,3,GNEWSAVillagers fight to save pub oak
OL,4,Atree from the axe
OL,5,
OL,6,FVillagers are campaigning to save a
OL,7,Flarge oak tree from the axe.
OL,9,FThe tree, which is estimated to be more
OL,10,Fthan 100 years old, grows on the
OL,11,Fgrounds of the Broad Oak pub in Main
OL,12,FStreet, Strelley.
OL,14,FGreene King, which owns the pub, wants
OL,15,Fto fell the tree after an inspection
OL,16,Ffound "significant structural and
OL,17,Fphysiological concerns", the Local
OL,18,FDemocracy Reporting Service reported.
OL,19,FThe tree is not the original oak that
OL,20,Fgave the pub its name.
OL,23,APub: 15-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,370,360,200,160,0,100
